{{!-- /the-faith-received/dictionary/ — a browsable reader for mo-tfr's
     v1/dtc/, the Dictionnaire de Théologie Catholique: a real French
     theological encyclopedia, not a short biographical glossary --
     entries run from a few hundred bytes to several megabytes. Nothing
     is translated in bulk. tfr-library worker's /v1/dtc-translate
     translates an entry the first time a reader opens it, caches the
     result, and serves the cache on every read after -- see
     assets/js/faith-dictionary.js and the file-header comment on
     dtcTranslate() in tfr-library/worker.js. Only letter A has landed
     in the source bucket as of 2026-09 and it is still growing; the
     browse UI works letter by letter regardless of how many have
     arrived, so nothing here needs to change when the rest lands. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/dictionary/">Dictionary</a></p>
      <h1>Dictionary</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub">The Dictionnaire de Théologie Catholique, translated as it is read &mdash; French and English side by side, article by article.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bband faith-feature-body">
    <div class="container">
      {{> "faith-received/_dictionary"}}
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<script src="{{asset "js/faith-dictionary.js"}}"></script>
